\section{Conclusions and Future Work}
\label{sec:conclusions}


Tokalatoer is an open-source toolkit that combines real-time context budget monitoring, interactive economic optimization, and reusable context engineering artifacts for AI coding assistants. It covers 15 models from three providers, implements prompt caching break-even analysis, supports three conversation cost strategies with formal cost models, and provides a VS~Code extension that makes token budgets visible. The current release (v3.1.1) includes model profiles, tab relevance scoring, pin/unpin/close controls, a context optimization engine, and 11 chat commands via \texttt{@tokalator}. The toolkit includes a comprehensive unit test suite with 124 test cases across 6 test files (see Appendix~\ref{app:tests}) covering pricing, caching, conversation simulation, context analysis, model profile integrity, and dashboard rendering, as well as a CI pipeline that runs build, lint, and test on every commit. 

Future work includes a secret detection guardrail (scanning open files for exposed credentials using regex patterns with severity tiers and a \texttt{/secrets} command), per-turn cost estimation with provider-specific prompt caching analysis and a \texttt{/cost} command, a multi-analyzer context optimization engine that produces scored health reports (planned for v3.1.5), team-wide context budget dashboards with CI/CD integration, a public token-counting REST API, a formal controlled user study (building on the preliminary feedback  on developers in Kariyer.net), calibration of the Cobb--Douglas sensitivity parameters from real usage data, and IDE support for Github Copilot (VS Code) at \url{https://tokalator.wiki} will continue to grow with automated wiki updates and community contributions to the catalog.

All components are MIT-licensed and available at \url{https://github.com/vfaraji89/tokalator}.

